<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Top-performing models still suffer from functional regression when non-functional instructions are added. <em id="S4.T2.19.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Base</em> is pass@1 on the original query. All other columns report the regression rate (%) relative to <em id="S4.T2.19.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Base</em>. <math id="S4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> Inst is the number of added instructions. <span id="S4.T2.19.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#D55C5A;">Light red</span> marks <math id="S4.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;5\%</annotation></semantics></math> regression and <span id="S4.T2.19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B00020;">deep red</span> denotes <math id="S4.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;10\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Full results for all 31 LLMs are listed in the Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Detailed Results for Functionality ‣ Appendix D Experiments ‣ Vibe Checker: Aligning Code Evaluationwith Human Preference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.07315v1/functional_comparison.svg" id="S4.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/214;" width="476" height="214"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Functional Regression Rate</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.07315v1/task_level_if_comparison.svg" id="S4.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/214;" width="476" height="214"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Task-Level Instruction Following</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Trends averaged over all evaluated models. As the number of instructions increases, functional regression grows steadily, while the task-level IF score drops markedly. Single-turn generation better preserves functionality, whereas multi-turn editing achieves higher instruction following.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
